  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\nIssued a flood watch for areas that have received heavy rainfall in\nrecent days and also are expected to get additional heavy rain into\ntonight. This combination is over portions of northern Kentucky and\ninto portions of southern Ohio. Precipitation will gradually start to\ndiminish overnight. Precipitation on Monday and Tuesday will be more\nlimited and primarily near and south of the Ohio River. There will be\nadditional precipitation chances for Wednesday primarily focused\nsouth of I-70. Drier conditions are expected for Thursday and Friday.\nThere is more uncertainty with model variability going into the \nweekend on precipitation chances.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2) \nHigh temperatures will be in the 70s to low 80s over the next week\nand lows will generally be in the 50s to low 60s for the week. These\nvalues are near normal for a lot of the week, however Tuesday through\nThursday will have a better chance of being slightly above normal for\ntemperatures.",
